Base model
----------

This model is a modified version of the tessdata_best Hebrew model
(heb.traineddata) of the Tesseract OCR project,
https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best, commit
e12c65a915945e4c28e237a9b52bc4a8f39a0cec, sha256
dbaa827aea6bc21215638447f17783a1004987c2d0bf5573d111fee397abdae5, licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

HeOCR modified it in two stages. HeOCR R7 (2026-11-11,
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24126448) fine-tuned its LSTM network on
real scanned Hebrew lines and added the maqaf U+05BE and the en dash U+2013
to its character set. oldprint-v1 (2026-11-18) continued training from R7's
weights on more real scanned lines and rendered born-digital lines. Its
character set and its dictionary components are R7's, unchanged. R7's
dictionary components were rebuilt from the base model's own word list with
build files from https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/langdata_lstm, commit
07930fd9f246622c26eb5de794d9212ceac432d3, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. No word list was built from any training text.

R7's training data, credited in R7's NOTICE, is part of this model's
lineage. That NOTICE is distributed with this model as NOTICE.r7 and must be
kept with it.

Software
--------

The model was trained with, and runs in, Tesseract 5.5.3
(https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. The model file contains no Tesseract code.

Training data: Internet Archive scans
-------------------------------------

Training lines were cut from these Internet Archive items
(https://archive.org/details/<identifier>), scans of public-domain books.
They were fetched from the Internet Archive (its metadata and IIIF
services), the route HeOCR's legal strategy calls internet_archive. The
Internet Archive publishes them without an explicit licence. The original
conditions of each item on the Internet Archive still apply. None comes
from NLI.

Each item passed HeOCR's Internet Archive rights gate
(hocrgen.fetchers.ia_iiif.decide_ia_rights; hocrgen decision
planning/decisions/2026-11-09-internet-archive-library-scans.md), and each
text aligned to it has its own rights justification
(hocrgen.rights_justification.v1; hocrgen decision
planning/decisions/2026-11-10-legal-strategy.md). In short: a public-domain
book, a faithful scan, fetched from the Internet Archive; no new right
arises in the scan and no contract binds its reuse. The justification ids
are listed in oldprint_v1_training_run.json.

Scans made by university libraries (source class
ia_library_scan_no_licence_field; none was digitized by Google):

  zikhronotlebetda01reck: Abraham Shalom Friedberg (d. 1902), Zikhronot
    le-Vet David. Warsaw, 1893. Robarts - University of Toronto. 6,099
    lines.
  midrashleaovhame0305tobi: Tobiah ben Eliezer, Midrash Lekach Tov, edited
    by Salomon Buber (d. 1906), vols 3-5. Vilna, 1884. Robarts - University
    of Toronto. 6,063 lines.
  kolkitveylkatsen018800: Judah Leib Katzenelson (d. 1917), Kol Kitve
    Y. L. Katsenelson. St Petersburg, 1905. University of Illinois
    Urbana-Champaign. 5,712 lines.
  seferhademaotmeo0000bern: Simon Bernfeld (d. 1940), Sefer ha-Dema'ot.
    Berlin, 1923. University of Toronto, Downsview. 5,350 lines.
  betnekhothahalak01horouoft: Bet Nekhot ha-Halakhot o Toratan shel
    Rishonim, part I, edited by Chaim Meir Horowitz. Frankfurt am Main,
    1881. Robarts - University of Toronto. 1,896 lines.

Google-class scans (source class ia_google_digitized_scan), retrieved via
the Internet Archive, not from Google or NLI. They are admitted under
hocrgen's legal strategy, rule 3 (Routes B and C: Google-digitized scans
fetched from the Internet Archive or Wikimedia Commons;
planning/decisions/2026-11-10-legal-strategy.md), and heocr-engine decision
0015 (planning/decisions/0015-legal-strategy.md). Google's front-page usage
guidelines are requests, not a contract, and HeOCR accepted no terms from
Google for these files. Hygiene (legal strategy, rule 5): any Google
front matter was excluded, and no "Digitized by Google" watermark was found on
any training page. Neither Google, the Open Siddur Project nor the
contributing library endorses HeOCR.

  afahleneemaniml00fngoog: Samuel Joseph Fuenn (d. 1891), Safah
    le-Ne'emanim. Vilna, 1881. Digitized by Google; retrieved via the
    Internet Archive; contributing library: University of California.
    5,749 lines.
  mahzor-vitri-abraham-berliner-1893: Simhah ben Samuel of Vitry, Machzor
    Vitry, edited by Simeon Hurwitz. Berlin: Mekize Nirdamim, 1889-1897.
    A copy the Open Siddur Project derived from a Google Books scan;
    retrieved via the Internet Archive. 6,077 lines.

Every author, editor and other named contributor of the books above died
more than 70 years ago, per their rights justifications, so the books are
in the public domain in Israel. Every book was printed before 1931 and is
also past the United States copyright term.

Training data: text
-------------------

The lines are labelled with these transcriptions, never with OCR:
  - Project Ben-Yehuda (https://benyehuda.org), public domain dump release
    2026-03 (https://github.com/projectbenyehuda/public_domain_dump), for
    the books by Friedberg, Katzenelson, Bernfeld and Fuenn. Its licence
    states that the data files are in the public domain. Credit: Project
    Ben-Yehuda volunteers.
  - Sefaria (https://www.sefaria.org), public-domain digital versions
    "Midrash Lekach Tov on Torah, Vilna 1884" and "Machzor Vitry, Berlin,
    1893-97", each citing the printing it transcribes.
  - Project Gutenberg ebook #43740 (https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/43740),
    public domain in the USA, produced by David T. Jones, Enrico Segre and
    Distributed Proofreaders Canada, for Bet Nekhot ha-Halakhot.

Training data: Reshumot (laws and regulations)
----------------------------------------------

40,000 training lines were rendered by HeOCR from born-digital PDF
booklets of ספר החוקים (Sefer ha-Hukim) and קובץ התקנות (Kovetz
ha-Takanot), published by Reshumot (רשומות), the official gazette of the
State of Israel, and labelled with the publisher's own PDF text layer for
each line. Laws and regulations carry no copyright in Israel (Copyright Act
2007, section 6; PD-IL). Their status outside Israel, including the United
States, is not asserted here. No line comes from an evaluation booklet. The
booklet identifiers are in oldprint_v1_training_run.json.

The model contains no scan images, no rendered pages and no text files.
The line crops are not distributed with it.

Evaluation data (not used for training)
---------------------------------------

The model was chosen on old-print page images with reference transcriptions
(HeOCR's audit2 dev pages), on development line sets whose references come
from Hebrew Wikisource (CC BY-SA 4.0, Hebrew Wikisource contributors),
Project Ben-Yehuda (public domain), Sefaria (public domain) and Reshumot
(PD-IL), and on HeOCR's open synthetic document sets. They were never
trained on. The model contains no evaluation text. Its accuracy is not
measured on a held-out set yet.

